<urn:atm:triage:finding/AJ7-RBQA-F002-REINVENTED-CONFIG-PATTERN>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AJ7-RBQA-F002-REINVENTED-CONFIG-PATTERN" ;
  triage:title "check_runtime_observation_boundary.py reinvents its own config format instead of following the mandated check_env_var_boundary.py pattern" ;
  triage:description "The sprint doc requires the tests to 'follow the existing environment-boundary guard configuration pattern with explicit required-positive file/symbol checks' -- i.e. check_env_var_boundary.py (463 lines, lint_common-integrated: discover_repo_root, load_lint_config, is_code_line, build_report/print_report, a .just/lint-config.toml [env_var_boundary] section, an allowlist TOML, and ~13 isolated-fixture unit tests). check_runtime_observation_boundary.py instead hardcodes ALLOWED/REQUIRED/TOKENS as bare Python literals in an un-importable main()-only script (63 lines), with no lint_common import, no TOML config, no allowlist file, and no extracted collection function to unit-test against -- which directly explains AJ7-ATM-QA-002 (there's no seam to write isolated fixture tests against). Confirmed by arch-qa and ruthless-boundary-qa via direct file comparison. QA source: PR #742, phase-aj-s7-qa-1." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AJ" ;
